From: Flux architecture integration
Subject: [PATCH] fork: pair architecture mmap preparation and completion

Prepare host COW before copy_page_range, under both mmap write locks.
Complete on every prepared exit, under the parent mmap write lock. The
optional completion supplies the fork TLB synchronization and can report
failure; architectures without it retain flush_tlb_mm unchanged.

Flux's host gate write-protects and flushes aliases. Keep those aliases
instead of revoking and reconstructing the entire parent address space.
Ordinary Linux invalidation paths are unchanged.

--- a/kernel/kernel/fork.c
+++ b/kernel/kernel/fork.c
@@ -664,6 +664,11 @@
 	 * Not linked in yet - no deadlock potential:
 	 */
 	mmap_write_lock_nested(mm, SINGLE_DEPTH_NESTING);
+#ifdef arch_dup_mmap_prepare
+	retval = arch_dup_mmap_prepare(oldmm, mm);
+	if (retval)
+		goto out;
+#endif
 
 	/* No ordering required: file already has been exposed. */
 	dup_mm_exe_file(mm, oldmm);
@@ -771,7 +776,11 @@
 		mt_set_in_rcu(vmi.mas.tree);
 out:
 	mmap_write_unlock(mm);
+#ifdef arch_dup_mmap_finish
+	retval = arch_dup_mmap_finish(oldmm, mm, retval);
+#else
 	flush_tlb_mm(oldmm);
+#endif
 	mmap_write_unlock(oldmm);
 	dup_userfaultfd_complete(&uf);
 fail_uprobe_end:
